               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate calendar="Gregorian" notAfter="1475" notBefore="1450">15th century, third quarter</origDate>
                     <origPlace cert="low">
                        <country key="place_1000080">Italy</country>, <settlement key="place_7004474">Naples</settlement> (?)<!--ORIGINAL: Italian, Naples (?)--></origPlace>
                  </origin>
                  
                  <provenance>Arms of the Paruta family of Venice with mitre and crozier. The same arms and mitre, etc., occur in the Broadley Pontifical, Harvard College, MS. Typ. 217, 
                  and a Missal (Sotheby's, 3 April 1957, lot 113), where they were identified as those of <persName role="fmo" key="person_126">Bartolomeo Paruta</persName>, 
                     abbot of S. Gregorio, Venice. The branch of the Paruta family in Sicily appears to have had different arms. 
                  Cf. <ref target="https://medieval.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/manuscript_3826">MS. Canon. Pat. Lat. 33</ref> and <ref target="https://medieval.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/manuscript_2255">MS. Canon. Class. Lat. 232</ref>
                  </provenance>
                  
                  <provenance>In the lower margin of <ref target="https://digital.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/objects/72708c99-1723-4b6b-8787-f7583cef3214/surfaces/15bb0a5d-5d1a-4277-9b35-3c421d26be53/">fol. 1r</ref>: the arms of a bishop: or on a chief gules 3 quatrefoils argent</provenance>
                  
                  <provenance><persName key="person_2384880" role="fmo">Matteo Luigi Canonici (1727– <hi rend="italic">c</hi>. 1806)</persName></provenance>
                  <provenance notAfter="1807" resp="#SC">Following Canonici's death, the collection passed to his brother, <persName key="person_446" role="fmo">Giuseppe Canonici</persName>, and 
                     then to Canonici's nephew, <persName role="fmo" key="person_431">Giovanni Perissinotti</persName>, in 1807 following Giuseppe Canonici's death</provenance>
                  <acquisition when="1817">Bought by the Bodleian Library in 1817 from Giovanni Perissinotti. On the purchase, see <ref target="https://digital.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/collections/canonici/">Digital Bodleian</ref></acquisition>
                  
               </history>
